OL,3,GNEWSAArtefacts dating back 500 years
OL,4,Afound at bridge
OL,5,
OL,6,FArtefacts dating back more than 500
OL,7,Fyears have been discovered during the
OL,8,Frestoration of a medieval
OL,9,FWorcestershire bridge.
OL,11,FAmong the most significant finds at
OL,12,FPowick Old Bridge, in Worcester, was a
OL,13,Frare copper alloy signet ring dating
OL,14,Ffrom the late 15th or 16th Century.
OL,16,FThe ring, believed to have been worn by
OL,17,Fa merchant, was recovered from river
OL,18,Fsilts downstream of the bridge. It was
OL,19,Fengraved with a reversed letter "R",
OL,20,Fwhich would have been used to create
OL,21,Fwax seals on letters.
OL,23,APub: 15-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
